      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Kivalina sits on the southern tip of a 12‑km barrier island between the Chukchi Sea and a lagoon at the mouth of the Kivalina River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kivalina%2C_Alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kivalina experiences a dry subarctic climate, bordering on tundra, with long, very cold winters and short, cool summers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kivalina%2C_Alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Kivalina is the only village in the region where people hunt the bowhead whale.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kivalina%2C_Alaska",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The island on which Kivalina lies is threatened by rising sea levels and coastal erosion caused by climate change.",
